# Architecture

## Layering

Prefer clear layers:

1. HTTP / API (FastAPI routes, schemas)
2. Application / services (orchestration)
3. Domain models (Pydantic / business rules)
4. Persistence (repositories, SQLAlchemy)
5. Providers (vendor SDKs such as OpenAI)

Dependencies point **inward/downward**. Lower layers must not import higher layers.

## Boundaries

- Infrastructure (providers, DB engines, frameworks) must not leak into domain models.
- Generic AI tooling (`schema`, `registry`, `validation`, `execution`) must stay **domain-neutral**.
- Concrete entity tools (e.g. Character) may depend on repositories/domain; generic tooling must not.

## Safety rules

- No reflection-based dispatch (`getattr`/`eval`/`globals`) to select callables.
- Call only explicitly registered bindings.
- Do not swallow unexpected errors with broad `except Exception` at tool execution boundaries.
- Expected domain/tool failures use explicit typed errors and predictable contracts.

## Dependency direction (AI stack)

```
Provider  ->  LLMService  ->  AgentService (future)
ToolDefinition / Registry / Validator / Executor  <-  AgentService (future)
CharacterTools  ->  CharacterRepository / Character domain
```

Generic tool layers must not import Character tools, repositories, FastAPI, or providers.
